MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Sticky Fingers and Exile On Main Street felt connected to my Clapton and Hendrix listening through their bluesy guitar and roots rock sound.",
    "Standing in the Breach was my strongest choice because reflective songwriting from an established artist fits what drew me toward You Should Be So Lucky."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The outlaw country collection and Donovan's folk-pop hits did not fit my current interest in rootsy rock, even though they come from familiar older music traditions.",
    "Blackstar's experimental direction was less appealing for my current mood, and I could not judge Retrospective confidently without knowing the artist."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections leaned too heavily on the idea that liking established rock artists means wanting any familiar classic release.",
    "Remasters, hits collections, and live recordings seemed to be treated as equally appealing next choices, although familiarity alone gives me little reason to choose them today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choices suggest interest in established musicians making fresh albums, which made the Browne album more compelling than another collection of older songs.",
    "A bluesy sound helps an album fit, but reflective songwriting and wanting to hear that particular release matter more when I choose just one album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in established rock musicians but leaned too much on familiar catalogs and too little on the specific album I want to hear now."
}
